<title>ITALY: Italy senate converts 'jobs pact' into law.</title>
<headline>Italy senate converts 'jobs pact' into law.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's upper house of parliament on Wednesday converted a so-called &quot;jobs pact&quot; draft law on labour market flexibility into law.</p>
<p>The measure, promoted by Labour Minister Tiziano Treu, is aimed at simplifying procedures to free up public expenditure on employment.</p>
<p>It completes provisions made in a September 1996 pact between government, unions and employers to boost jobs.</p>
<p>Wednesday's vote of approval in the senate ended five months of parliamentary debate on the measure.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom 39 6 678 2501</p>
</text>
